riscos-mesa: faster GLSL/ARB shaders, with exactly the same results.

- The batch interpreter (_mesa_execute_program_batch, generated by
  tools/gen-glsl-batch.py) gets fast paths for instructions that write
  only .x or only .xyz with a component-wise opcode (ABS ADD CMP FLR FRC
  LRP MAD MAX MIN MOV MUL SGE SLT SSG SUB TRUNC): only the written
  components are fetched and computed. Most of a compiled fragment
  shader's instructions write a single component, and the general path
  computed all four and then masked. Each component is the same
  expression on the same inputs, so every result is bit-identical.
- decoded_matches compares the cached instructions a word at a time
  instead of with memcmp: UnixLib's memcmp is a byte loop, and this check
  runs for every span and vertex batch.

--- a/src/mesa/program/prog_execute.c
+++ b/src/mesa/program/prog_execute.c
@@ -547,6 +547,29 @@
